# Context

Users propose features; the GitHub Actions workflow `agent.yml` regularly
screens proposals against `constitution.md` and implements the first one that
passes. Spending credentials exist only in that workflow — never in the app,
never on the VPS.

Proposals are **GitHub Issues**, created by the app with a fine-grained
Issues-only token. Votes are the 👍/👎 reactions on the issue (👍 +1, 👎 −1).
Issues authored by anyone else, and all issue comments, are ignored.

