Deliver pushes the branch, opens a PR with `Closes #<issue>`, and enables
auto-merge (squash). Once the `test` check passes GitHub merges it — there is no
human review, so preflight is the last gate — the push to `main` deploys, and
the issue closes. A PR that closes without merging frees its issue again. If you
cannot implement the feature, exit without committing: no PR, proposal stays
open.

# Frozen — never modify

`check-frozen.sh` fails the `test` check if any of these change, and CI runs the
base ref's copy, so the gate cannot be edited in the PR it gates.

- **`constitution.md`** — the rules the app lives by; the homepage links to it.
- **`scripts/locked/`** — the whole directory: no edits, deletions, or
  additions. It holds the agent loop, these prompts, `smoke.sh`,
  `check-frozen.sh`, the VPS lifecycle scripts, and the payment code — the only
  code that ever touches `WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY`.
- **`.github/workflows/`** — they hold the spend and SSH credentials. To change
  how the app builds or deploys, edit `scripts/deploy.sh`, which runs on the VPS
  where no spend keys exist.

Everything else is yours: `app/`, `scripts/preflight.sh`, `scripts/deploy.sh`,
`docker-compose.yml`, and `AGENTS.md`.

# Rules

- **Keep `smoke.sh` passing.** Proposal intake and voting are life support
  (`POST /api/proposals` → 201; the vote endpoints keep their origin/method
  guards). Features may change how they look, never remove them.
- Keep `secrets.env`, `*.env` holding private keys, and `*.key` out of commits
  and logs.
- Never push directly to `main`.
- The site is reachable only through Cloudflare — Caddy requires a Cloudflare
  origin-pull client certificate, and edge rate limiting is zone state written
  once at init.
- Keep changes in `app/` unless the feature genuinely needs infra.
- Be terse: act, don't narrate. Prefer tool calls and code edits over prose.

